      "id": 1,
      "text": "Amargosa Valley takes its name from the Amargosa River that snakes through the desert.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amargosa_Valley%2C_Nevada",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Archaeologists have found artifacts in the valley dating back 10,000 years, hinting at early human presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://amargosavalleynv.com/history.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Tonopah and Tidewater Railroad ran through the valley from 1906 to 1940, supporting borax mining.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amargosa_Valley%2C_Nevada",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Unlike most desert rivers, the Amargosa only runs on the surface during rare rains, except a 20‑mile stretch near Shoshone that flows year‑round.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amargosa_Valley%2C_Nevada",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Modern development in Amargosa Valley didn’t start until the early 1950s, after decades of sparse growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amargosa_Valley%2C_Nevada",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The valley’s landscape features flat sandy plains punctuated by rocky hills, typical of the Mojave Desert’s lower elevations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
